[{:db/id "q-87555/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "6bddf287-3d2f-5d6c-bdd7-c25314522951" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87555/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "96fda114-dcbb-5232-9f0c-2e3aa047cccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87555/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "c0d22426-d7c1-5b4b-b092-a162e8ec889d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87555/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "5ca39ae5-7696-5a74-a652-4cd2c74356c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87555/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "797cd1bb-e701-582e-8154-900c18ef4a3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87555/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "95734b0d-e3a4-52b3-84f0-67d4358c908e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87555/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer-field/choices ["q-87555/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-87555/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-87555/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" "q-87555/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-87555/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87555" :question/id #uuid "fdede67c-f471-5920-9cab-83156b3bc645" :question/math-academy-id "q-87555" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $5$ data points, where \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}=-20,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}^{2}=170.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=5$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}=-20,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-20) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}^{2}=170,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 170 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =34-{(-4)}^{2} \\\\  & =34-16 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87555/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87555"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87564/selection/0d85b4ee108293439822ced80dcafe1f03c5665b8e950012ad8d0f1824d1ad22" :answer/id #uuid "550f48bf-5654-5873-9ba3-becbf00e2303" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{201}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87564/selection/6458db705a47336256e36e13a5926dd604e31fbd97f13bec2bfef71207c7dad7" :answer/id #uuid "ba49ac96-1b10-5726-899a-fdfc1fe5ffe7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{22}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87564/selection/92bb7ca444257063292d20189417b7ff93ff5d535bc0fc717ec11a2516e511be" :answer/id #uuid "b343ba78-459a-56fd-bc4b-c7623bc1d000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{97}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87564/selection/c5837d19dcca7502583d2f58fec24deef22c2021f6d18a3455d7a5aeaa6ef7ba" :answer/id #uuid "7be09378-785d-54da-8734-24a4297b8e7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{26}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87564/selection/30b10a7494becfea4386590437c933a1167ec6d54b025e8e1b827170c9c7819a" :answer/id #uuid "34286e4e-d2ff-545e-b707-351f6be66535" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{46}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87564/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aafbb48a-1541-5ce4-8eb5-dd690d367b74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87564/selection/c5837d19dcca7502583d2f58fec24deef22c2021f6d18a3455d7a5aeaa6ef7ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-87564/selection/0d85b4ee108293439822ced80dcafe1f03c5665b8e950012ad8d0f1824d1ad22" "q-87564/selection/6458db705a47336256e36e13a5926dd604e31fbd97f13bec2bfef71207c7dad7" "q-87564/selection/92bb7ca444257063292d20189417b7ff93ff5d535bc0fc717ec11a2516e511be" "q-87564/selection/c5837d19dcca7502583d2f58fec24deef22c2021f6d18a3455d7a5aeaa6ef7ba" "q-87564/selection/30b10a7494becfea4386590437c933a1167ec6d54b025e8e1b827170c9c7819a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87564" :question/id #uuid "e8b07372-077f-5153-9127-d4780e7f794c" :question/math-academy-id "q-87564" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $7$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=35,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=201.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=35,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 35 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=201,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 201 \\\\  & =\\frac{201}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{201}{7}-{(5)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{201}{7}-25 \\\\  & =\\frac{201-175}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87564/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87564"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263422/field-1/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991" :answer/id #uuid "0e34cd32-bdd9-5982-92d6-d8c373fb531a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263422/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "56179feb-ba3d-5788-94a3-2da70f22fed1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263422/field-1/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991" :answer-field/choices ["q-263422/field-1/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263422" :question/id #uuid "d82643ef-6cc2-55a0-9bd5-f1cb4429693c" :question/math-academy-id "q-263422" :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n-18,\\,-11,\\,-8,\\,4,\\,6,\\,-3\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-18-11-8+4+6-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-30) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot ((-18)^{2}+(-11)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (324+121+64+16+36+9) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 570 \\\\  & =\\frac{570}{6} \\\\  & =95.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =95-{(-5)}^{2} \\\\  & =95-25 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-263422/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0040fc1-2134-5eaa-a3e8-6c7a457f75f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263422"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263451/field-1/4e456dabe03ea095e00f782d8a4246023bf40bb3df58268496f3da803674ceef" :answer/id #uuid "e61e7f97-98d1-5e60-b965-3c4b6b96c7b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{38}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263451/field-1/ff719fe6e9f394f14c4ef7f13ec8dc8641132e81c0acb9899b233b18e63ce753" :answer/id #uuid "d968abf2-e650-585c-9021-6d98031f7510" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{38}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263451/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "efbe38a0-c7c6-5108-b180-f56d2527b1d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263451/field-1/4e456dabe03ea095e00f782d8a4246023bf40bb3df58268496f3da803674ceef" :answer-field/choices ["q-263451/field-1/4e456dabe03ea095e00f782d8a4246023bf40bb3df58268496f3da803674ceef" "q-263451/field-1/ff719fe6e9f394f14c4ef7f13ec8dc8641132e81c0acb9899b233b18e63ce753"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263451" :question/id #uuid "0b72f295-29a5-54b1-8266-2fadea925b1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-263451" :question/problem "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n10,\\,14,\\,16,\\,9,\\,12,\\,5\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (10+14+16+9+12+5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 66 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot [{10}^{2}+{14}^{2}+{16}^{2}+{9}^{2}+{12}^{2}+{5}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot [100+196+256+81+144+25] \\\\  & =\\frac{802}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{401}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{401}{3}-{(11)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{401}{3}-121 \\\\  & =\\frac{401-363}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{38}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-263451/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a72dae6-2bbf-5e59-b71d-8ee57f589753"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263451"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263584/field-1/79ce3826cd4ec8b2e58408e7219722f0290fe10fa24561c5e4638ad5c1fec66d" :answer/id #uuid "b28a352e-eea2-590b-88cd-d7767e1fa27d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{172}{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263584/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c64242b2-f6fd-514c-b8a8-ece150a2164f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263584/field-1/79ce3826cd4ec8b2e58408e7219722f0290fe10fa24561c5e4638ad5c1fec66d" :answer-field/choices ["q-263584/field-1/79ce3826cd4ec8b2e58408e7219722f0290fe10fa24561c5e4638ad5c1fec66d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263584" :question/id #uuid "d8be7b41-0f98-5531-8d7e-13afd6a9cc59" :question/math-academy-id "q-263584" :question/problem "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n9,\\,4,\\,15,\\,14,\\,18,\\,7,\\,17\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (9+4+15+14+18+7+17) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 84 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [{9}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{15}^{2}+{14}^{2}+{18}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{17}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [81+16+225+196+324+49+289] \\\\  & =\\frac{1180}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1180}{7}-{(12)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1180}{7}-144 \\\\  & =\\frac{1180-1008}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{172}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{172}{7}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{43}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-263584/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a72dae6-2bbf-5e59-b71d-8ee57f589753"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263584"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
